{% comment %}
  Universal condition care page. Drives /pages/fungal-acne,
  /pages/seb-derm-dandruff, and /pages/tinea-versicolor from a single
  section file. All condition-specific copy is set in the case block
  at the top; the rest of the section uses those variables.

  Structure (Nurx-inspired but care-focused):
    1. Hero
    2. Trust bar
    3. What it is (plain-language explainer)
    4. Symptoms checklist
    5. How Kyn Skyn treats it
    6. What's included
    7. The process (4 steps)
    8. Pricing summary (links to full pricing on consultation page)
    9. Condition-specific FAQ
    10. Final CTA
{% endcomment %}

{%- case page.handle -%}
  {%- when 'fungal-acne' -%}
    {%- assign condition_name = 'Fungal Acne' -%}
    {%- assign condition_subtitle = "Tiny, itchy bumps that won't go away." -%}
    {%- assign hero_heading = 'Clear the bumps.' -%}
    {%- assign hero_sub = "It's a yeast condition, not acne. The right antifungal clears it. A simple routine keeps it clear." -%}
    {%- assign condition_slug = 'fungal-acne' -%}
    {%- assign condition_photo = 'kiiren-closeup.jpg' -%}
    {%- assign condition_photo_position = 'right 30%' -%}
    {%- assign whatitis_heading = 'A yeast condition that looks like acne' -%}
    {%- assign whatitis_p1 = '<em>Malassezia folliculitis</em> is an inflammatory infection of the hair follicle caused by <em>Malassezia</em>, a yeast that lives on nearly all human skin. When the local environment shifts, the yeast can overgrow inside the follicle and trigger an immune response. The result is a cluster of small, often itchy bumps people mistake for acne.' -%}
    {%- assign whatitis_p2 = 'Standard acne treatments do not target yeast and often make fungal acne worse. Many of them also contain ingredients <em>Malassezia</em> feeds on. Years of misdiagnosis is the rule, not the exception.' -%}
    {%- assign whatitis_p3 = "The fix is straightforward once it's named: an antifungal that actually targets <em>Malassezia</em>, paired with a routine that doesn't feed it." -%}
    {%- assign symptoms_heading = 'Signs you might have fungal acne' -%}
    {%- assign symptoms_csv = 'Uniform small bumps that look almost identical|Itchiness, especially after sweating|Breakouts on the forehead, hairline, jawline, chest, or upper back|Acne treatments (benzoyl peroxide, antibiotics) made it worse|Flares with heat, humidity, or after antibiotic courses' -%}
    {%- assign treatment_heading = 'How we treat fungal acne' -%}
    {%- assign treatment_p1 = 'Your provider reviews your photos and intake, confirms the diagnosis, and prescribes a topical antifungal (e.g., ketoconazole) where needed. From there, the treatment plan covers the routine that keeps the yeast in check long-term, not just clearing the current flare.' -%}
    {%- assign recommended_plan = 'quarterly' -%}
    {%- assign recommended_plan_label = 'Quarterly Treatment Plan' -%}
    {%- assign recommended_reason = 'Fungal acne almost always relapses without an ongoing routine. Most people stay clear with the Quarterly Plan, which covers the maintenance phase.' -%}
    {%- assign final_cta_heading = 'Ready to actually treat it?' -%}
    {%- assign final_cta_sub = 'Submit your intake, get a written diagnosis from a licensed clinician, and start a treatment plan that targets the actual cause.' -%}
    {%- assign payoff_csv = "Clear bumps, for real this time~A prescription that targets the actual cause, not the wrong category.|A routine that fits real life~Two products, not seven. Built to keep flares from coming back.|Skincare that doesn't fight your treatment~Products that won't feed the yeast you're working to clear." -%}

  {%- when 'seb-derm-dandruff' -%}
    {%- assign condition_name = 'Seb Derm & Dandruff' -%}
    {%- assign condition_subtitle = 'Flaky patches and an itchy scalp that won\'t quit.' -%}
    {%- assign hero_heading = 'Stop the flakes.' -%}
    {%- assign hero_sub = "It's a yeast that thrives on oily skin. The right antifungal clears it. A simple routine keeps it clear." -%}
    {%- assign condition_slug = 'seb-derm-dandruff' -%}
    {%- assign condition_photo = 'gabby-closeup.jpg' -%}
    {%- assign condition_photo_position = 'right 25%' -%}
    {%- assign whatitis_heading = 'Inflammation triggered by yeast in oily skin' -%}
    {%- assign whatitis_p1 = 'Seborrheic dermatitis is a chronic inflammatory condition driven by <em>Malassezia</em>, the same yeast behind fungal acne and dandruff. It typically shows up where your skin produces the most oil: scalp, around the nose, eyebrows, behind the ears, and the upper chest.' -%}
    {%- assign whatitis_p2 = 'Dandruff is essentially scalp seb derm with less inflammation. They sit on the same spectrum, respond to the same treatment, and the line between them is fuzzy.' -%}
    {%- assign whatitis_p3 = "Most people have been told it's &ldquo;just dry skin&rdquo; and given a moisturizer that makes it worse. The actual fix is an antifungal active that brings the yeast back into balance, then a maintenance routine that holds." -%}
    {%- assign symptoms_heading = 'Signs you might have seb derm or dandruff' -%}
    {%- assign symptoms_csv = 'Flaky or scaly patches on scalp, eyebrows, sides of nose, or chest|Redness that comes and goes, often with itch|Greasy or powdery scale, sometimes mistaken for dryness|Itchy scalp with persistent flakes that anti-dandruff shampoo barely touches|Worse with stress, weather changes, or certain hair products' -%}
    {%- assign treatment_heading = 'How we treat seb derm and dandruff' -%}
    {%- assign treatment_p1 = 'Your provider reviews your photos and intake, confirms the diagnosis, and prescribes a topical antifungal (e.g., ketoconazole) for the affected zones. The treatment plan also includes the maintenance schedule, scalp and skin care choices, and what to do when triggers hit.' -%}
    {%- assign recommended_plan = 'quarterly' -%}
    {%- assign recommended_plan_label = 'Quarterly Treatment Plan' -%}
    {%- assign recommended_reason = "Seb derm and dandruff are chronic. The Quarterly Plan covers ongoing care so you're not starting over every flare." -%}
    {%- assign final_cta_heading = 'Get out of the flake-and-flare loop.' -%}
    {%- assign final_cta_sub = 'Submit your intake, get a written diagnosis, and start a treatment plan that holds.' -%}
    {%- assign payoff_csv = "Flakes and itch gone, not just hidden~An antifungal that hits the cause, plus a routine that holds long after.|Triggers stop wrecking your skin~A maintenance plan built for stress, weather, and product changes.|Care from someone who's seen it~A clinician who treats seb derm every day, not once a year." -%}

  {%- when 'tinea-versicolor' -%}
    {%- assign condition_name = 'Tinea Versicolor' -%}
    {%- assign condition_subtitle = "Spots that won't tan with the rest of your skin." -%}
    {%- assign hero_heading = 'Even out the patches.' -%}
    {%- assign hero_sub = "It's a yeast condition that flares with heat. We treat the cause and keep it from coming back." -%}
    {%- assign condition_slug = 'tinea-versicolor' -%}
    {%- assign condition_photo = 'kwamena-smile.jpg' -%}
    {%- assign condition_photo_position = 'right 20%' -%}
    {%- assign whatitis_heading = "Yeast that disrupts the skin's pigment production" -%}
    {%- assign whatitis_p1 = 'Tinea versicolor is caused by <em>Malassezia</em> overgrowing on the skin and producing compounds that interfere with melanin production in the affected areas. The result is patches that are lighter or darker than your surrounding skin, often most visible after sun exposure.' -%}
    {%- assign whatitis_p2 = "It's common, harmless to your overall health, and very treatable. With the right antifungal, the yeast clears. The discoloration itself takes time to even out, since pigment production needs time to recover." -%}
    {%- assign whatitis_p3 = 'It tends to come back during hot, humid months. A maintenance routine cuts down the frequency.' -%}
    {%- assign symptoms_heading = 'Signs you might have tinea versicolor' -%}
    {%- assign symptoms_csv = "Light or dark patches on chest, back, shoulders, or upper arms|Patches that don't tan with the rest of your skin|Fine, powdery scale when scratched|More visible in summer or after sun exposure|Returning year after year, especially in heat or humidity" -%}
    {%- assign treatment_heading = 'How we treat tinea versicolor' -%}
    {%- assign treatment_p1 = 'Your provider reviews your photos and intake, confirms the diagnosis, and prescribes a topical antifungal (e.g., ketoconazole). The cause clears with a course of treatment. Pigment evens out gradually as your skin recovers, and an ongoing routine keeps the patches from coming back when humidity hits.' -%}
    {%- assign recommended_plan = 'monthly' -%}
    {%- assign recommended_plan_label = 'Monthly Treatment Plan' -%}
    {%- assign recommended_reason = 'Tinea versicolor flares seasonally for most people, especially during heat and humidity. The Monthly Treatment Plan covers ongoing monitoring with your clinician, prescription refills as needed, and a maintenance routine that cuts down how often it comes back.' -%}
    {%- assign final_cta_heading = 'Clear the patches, keep them clear.' -%}
    {%- assign final_cta_sub = 'Submit your intake, get a written diagnosis, and start an ongoing plan that clears the patches and keeps them from coming back.' -%}
    {%- assign payoff_csv = "Patches even back out~The yeast clears, and your skin's pigment production catches up.|Stay clear through every summer~A maintenance plan built for the heat and humidity that bring it back.|A specialist who's seen this~A clinician familiar with how tinea looks across all skin tones." -%}

{%- endcase -%}

{%- assign symptoms = symptoms_csv | split: '|' -%}

<style>
  /* ========== HERO ========== */
  .cc-hero {
    position: relative;
    padding: 9rem 3rem 6rem;
    background: var(--dark);
    color: var(--cream);
    overflow: hidden;
    min-height: 32rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .cc-hero__bg {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 0;
  }

  .cc-hero__bg img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .cc-hero__overlay {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 1;
    background: linear-gradient(95deg,
      rgba(42, 2, 8, 0.92) 0%,
      rgba(42, 2, 8, 0.82) 35%,
      rgba(100, 18, 32, 0.55) 75%,
      rgba(100, 18, 32, 0.35) 100%
    );
  }

  .cc-hero__container {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 3;
    max-width: 64rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    width: 100%;
  }

  /* 3D plus-grid motif on the right side of the hero. Static, decorative. */
  .cc-hero__motif {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    right: -4rem;
    bottom: 0;
    width: clamp(22rem, 38vw, 40rem);
    z-index: 2;
    pointer-events: none;
    perspective: 1400px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .cc-hero__motif-stack {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;
    transform: rotateX(18deg) rotateY(-28deg);
  }

  .cc-hero__motif-layer {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    fill: currentColor;
  }

  .cc-hero__motif-layer--back {
    color: var(--terracotta);
    opacity: 0.22;
    transform: translateZ(-80px) scale(1.18);
    filter: blur(4px);
  }

  .cc-hero__motif-layer--mid {
    color: var(--gold);
    opacity: 0.45;
    transform: translateZ(-35px) scale(1.07);
  }

  .cc-hero__motif-layer--front {
    color: var(--gold);
    opacity: 0.85;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 24px 40px rgba(199, 91, 42, 0.4));
  }

  .cc-hero__eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-accent);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
  }

  .cc-hero__heading {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 5.5vw, 4.5rem);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
    max-width: 36rem;
  }

  .cc-hero__sub {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.5vw, 1.15rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
    opacity: 0.78;
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .cc-hero__sub em { font-style: italic; }

  .cc-hero__cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    padding: 1.05rem 2rem;
    background: var(--cream);
    color: var(--maroon);
    font-family: var(--font-accent);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: 999px;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 30px -10px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
    transition: transform 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease;
  }

  .cc-hero__cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 18px 40px -12px rgba(0,0,0,0.6);
  }

  .cc-hero__cta svg { width: 18px; height: 18px; transition: transform 0.3s; }
  .cc-hero__cta:hover svg { transform: translateX(3px); }

  /* ========== PAYOFF ========== */
  .cc-payoff {
    background: var(--cream);
    padding: 4.5rem 3rem;
  }

  .cc-payoff__container {
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .cc-payoff__eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--maroon);
    opacity: 0.55;
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cc-payoff__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 2.5rem 3rem;
  }

  .cc-payoff__item {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(100, 18, 32, 0.18);
